# =====================================================================
# Release V159 -- Stripe: link a practice to its Stripe Customer
# =====================================================================
# Adds Billing.Account_Billing.Stripe_Customer_ID (varchar(64) NULL), the only schema change the
# payment rail needs. The Customer is created lazily the first time a practice saves a card.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT A STRIPE SUBSCRIPTION. Billing.usp_Generate_Invoice_Lines stays the sole system
# of record for what is owed -- date-ranged per-seat prices, pro-rated first month, the trial as
# the Access_From -> Paid_From gap, affiliate commission. Stripe only collects. Modelling the
# seats as a Stripe Subscription would put a second engine on the same number, and the two would
# drift the first time a price changed mid-month.
#
# VAT: prices in Billing.Profile_Pricing are NET (full 50.00, clinician 20.00, front_office 5.00
# -> 60 / 24 / 6 gross at 20%). VAT is applied as a Stripe tax rate when the invoice is issued and
# is never stored in SQL, so the tax treatment can change without touching the billing engine.
# Nothing has ever been invoiced (zero rows in Billing.Invoice_Line, and the only account has
# Paid_From = 2100-01-01), so this costs no migration.
#
# SAFE TO DEPLOY AHEAD OF THE KEYS. The column is nullable and unused until a card is saved; the
# app fails closed without stripe-secret-key-<env> in Key Vault, and refuses outright if the key
# does not match the environment (dev must hold sk_test_, prod sk_live_).
#
# Guarded ALTER, so it is idempotent and safe to re-run.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V159__stripe_customer_on_account_billing.manifest
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY   Fabric\Billing.Account_Billing.Table.sql

TEST
